\label{thm:stable}
  Every $C\in B(H_1)\otimes_{\min}B(H_2)$ is stable.
  More generally, for every $C\in B(H_1\otimes H_2)$, any two iterated limits of $\varphi_C$ differ by at most $2\operatorname{dist}\bigl(C,B(H_1)\odot B(H_2)\bigr)$.

We show that \textup{(1)} and \textup{(2)} are equivalent and imply \textup{(3)}.
  The equivalence of (1) and (2) is \cref{lem:preservation}(d).

  For the implication from (1) to (3), the idea is that a weak cluster point of a sequence of effective observables must be the operator $Z_{\omega_1}$, and that any failure of this is a ladder.
