For $F$, take $\mathcal{H}=S_2(K)$, $a(\tau)=\tau$ and $b(\tau')=\tau'^*$, so that $\langle\tau,\tau'^*\rangle_{S_2}=\operatorname{Tr}(\tau'\tau)$;
  since $\|\tau\|_2\le\|\tau\|_1$, we have $R_a\le1$ and $\|b\|\le1$.
  On states, we have $T_{P_\pm}(\rho)=\frac12(I\pm T_F(\rho))$, and correspondingly $Z^{P_\pm}_{\omega_1}=\frac12(I\pm Z^F_{\omega_1})$, so the error for $P_\pm$ is half the error for $F$.
  For $[A=B]$, take $\mathcal{H}=\ell^2$, $a(\tau)=(\operatorname{Tr}\tau\Pi^A_\lambda)_\lambda$ and $b(\tau')=(\overline{\operatorname{Tr}\tau'\Pi^B_\lambda})_\lambda$;
  then $\|a(\tau)\|_2\le\sum_\lambda|\operatorname{Tr}\tau\Pi^A_\lambda|\le\|\tau\|_1$, and similarly for $b$.

\label{prop:sigmaadditive}
  Let $\mu$ be a countably additive Borel probability measure on $\mathfrak{D}(H_1)$, with the trace norm, and let $\nu$ be a mean on $\mathfrak{D}(H_2)$.
  Then for every $C\in B(H_1\otimes H_2)$, the two iterated integrals of $\varphi_C$ against $\mu$ and $\nu$ agree.

